{"message":"I have not opened the savings account or initiated any transfer. Your external $25,000 funding plan is noted, and no funds will be taken from the Green Account.

The highest available rate for the plan you described is the Gold Account’s 5.5% base APY. When paired with your Green Account, it receives the published +0.75% checking-linked boost, for a total APY of 6.25%. At $25,000 maintained for a year, that is approximately $1,562.50 in interest before any applicable tax considerations. The Gold Account compounds interest daily, requires a $5,000 opening deposit, and has a $10,000 ongoing minimum balance.

I can’t open it today because personal savings eligibility requires an active checking account held for at least 14 days. Your Green Account was opened today, so you should become eligible on 11/28/2025, assuming all accounts remain in good standing and you have fewer than five personal savings accounts. Once eligible, you can fund the Gold Account externally with the full $25,000; you’ll have 30 days to fund the account after opening."}

{"message":"I’m unable to submit the personal Silver Rewards Card application from this service because I couldn’t find an approved Rho-Bank procedure or application tool for personal credit-card applications. Your identity is already verified, and I have not submitted an application or changed any accounts.

The Silver Rewards Card remains the documented option matching your travel requirement: up to $15,000 in per-trip travel-insurance coverage when the eligible fare is charged in full, subject to policy terms and exclusions. If approved and later paired with your Gold Account, its +0.20% bonus would bring the projected combined APY to 6.45% with your Green Account’s +0.75% boost.

Would you like me to transfer you to a human agent to handle the card application?"}
